From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r9700-serving gfx1201 tuning
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gfx1201 unified-attention tuning + bf16 small-Q LDS guard
 (config-tree rebase)

Version-locked to AITER_REF=v0.1.25 (verified `git apply --check`
clean on v0.1.25, 2026-10-12; rebased from the v0.1.23/v0.1.24/post1
variant, which additionally carried a 2D prefill key dropped here —
see below). RDNA4-local launch-config tuning, not an
upstream cherry-pick. Replaces unified-attention-gfx1201-tune.patch AND
unified-attention-bf16-kv.patch from the v0.1.20.post1 era: v0.1.22
moved all UA launch config into the per-arch JSON config tree
(#4761/#5106 — select_2d_config/select_3d_config are gone), and v0.1.23
carries the upstream LDS guard #4868, so both code patches are retired.
Re-check after any AITER_REF bump: run tools/tune_ua_config.py and
re-run the e2e bench (see benchmarks/2026-08-25_gfx1201_ua_tuning.md).
Leading comments are ignored by `git apply` (Dockerfile.fullbuild
applies these with plain `git apply`).

What this carries, as additive gfx1201 DEFAULT.json keys (upstream
entries untouched; lookup precedence verified key-by-key):
- attn_3d D_LEQ_256.DT_any_bf16: num_warps 4, waves_per_eu 6 (BLOCK_M 16,
  stages 1 = upstream D_LEQ_1024.DT_any_bf16 values). The measured win:
  4 warps + 6 waves gives ~1.4x decode at 16k-128k context, identical
  output. Head-256 bf16 decode lands here (D_LEQ_128 misses at D=256,
  D_LEQ_1024 would match next); narrower shapes keep upstream values.
- attn_2d Q_LEQ_1.DT_any_bf16: Q_LEQ_1 copy with TILE_SIZE_MAX 64->32.
  Narrowed successor of the retired bf16-kv LDS cap: upstream #4868
  bounds the prefill bucket (Q_GEQ_256 MAX 32) but leaves the small-Q
  2D bucket at 64, which stages 2*64*256*2+scratch > 64 KiB for
  head-256 bf16 (the exact ROCm/aiter#4329 shape). Restores the old
  TILE-32 protection for exactly that bucket; every other bucket keeps
  upstream bounds.

Dropped on the v0.1.25 rebase (2026-10-12): the old attn_2d
Q_GEQ_256.DT_bf16_bf16 warps-8 key (~7% on 2048-token bf16 prefill under
the v0.1.24.post1 tree). v0.1.25 merged upstream #5790, which adds D/SW
schema axes: D-axis-first lookup now always prefers upstream's narrower
D_LEQ_* keys for every realistic shape, so the old key is unreachable —
and direct measurement (post1 kernels, D=256/Q=2048 bf16, 3 runs) shows
upstream's operative D_LEQ_256.Q_GEQ_64.DT_bf16_any (w4/s1/eu2, TILE 16)
beats it 1.06x on long-context chunked prefill (p2k_c64k; ties 1.02x on
short p2k). A w8/eu6/TILE-16 hybrid collapses to 0.78x, so the two
cannot be combined — take upstream's key as-is. Raw:
  ~/.vllm-workspace/ua_compare125.json. If a future tree re-opens this
  bucket, re-tune before re-adding.

diff --git a/aiter/ops/triton/configs/gfx1201/triton/attention/unified_attention/DEFAULT.json b/aiter/ops/triton/configs/gfx1201/triton/attention/unified_attention/DEFAULT.json
